The stock adapter uses publicly reachable data exposed to the UniFi Store
frontend. That integration can change without notice. GearBeacon does not
bypass authentication, rate limits, or anti-bot controls.

GearBeacon can integrate with GitHub Releases, Expo Push, ntfy, and Discord.
Those external services have their own terms, availability, and configuration
requirements.

During design, the MIT-licensed open-source project
"jamesccupps/UnifiStockWatcher" was consulted as a reference for UniFi Store
behavior. GearBeacon's source code was developed independently rather than
copied from that project.
